It shares benchmark matrices and licensing alignment with
[DistQLDPC](https://github.com/guluchen/DistQLDPC).

2. Benchmark matrices (`data/`)
-------------------------------

Matrix files follow the DistQLDPC layout: `{stem}_Hx.txt`, `_Hz.txt`, `_Gx.txt`,
`_Gz.txt` (GF(2), space-separated 0/1 rows). In this repository they live under
difficulty-tier subdirectories `data/tier0/` … `data/tier5/` (tier table in
data/README.md). Use `--stems-dir data` (recursive search) or a single tier folder
such as `data/tier0/`.

**Stem naming in this repository:** `{family}_{n}_{k}_{d}` where `n` is code length,
`k` is the number of logical qubits (from precomputed logical operators), and `d` is
the certified minimum distance when known. If `d` is not certified, the stem carries the
current proven bounds, `{lb}to{ub}` or `ge{lb}` (e.g. `TN_360_4_17to24`);
earlier stems used `unknown`.
Matrix data rows are unchanged; only filenames were aligned with benchmark metadata.

